# American English: only the lines that differ from English. The rest is English.

settings-thanks-project-serde-quick-xml-flate2 = Reading the app catalogs

settings-thanks-where-copyright = The licenses are in /usr/share/doc/trindle/copyright and THIRD-PARTY.txt.

settings-thanks-included-spellbook-where = Used as published, with no changes. Its source is at github.com/helix-editor/spellbook. Read the license in /usr/share/doc/trindle/copyright and THIRD-PARTY.txt.

settings-thanks-included-trindle-sans-where = The pound sign comes from Radio Canada. Its license is in /usr/share/fonts/truetype/trindle-sans/.

settings-thanks-included-emoji-and-spelling-lists-where = The emoji font uses the SIL Open Font License. The spelling lists have their own licenses. Read them in /usr/share/doc/ under each package's name.

settings-thanks-included-voice-control-where = Both are downloaded to this computer only when you switch on voice control. Their licenses are in the folder they are downloaded to.

settings-thanks-included-firmware-where = Each maker has its own license. Read it in /usr/share/doc/ under each firmware package's name, for example firmware-mediatek.

settings-thanks-licences = Licenses

settings-thanks-licences-about = What Trindle includes or started from has its own license.
